    "created_at": "2023-11-29T15:09:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-11-29T15:09:07Z",
    "body": "I believe the spec is leaving the control in a linear scale on purpose, so, as I mentioned [here](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5501#issuecomment-890523316), developers could choose the desired range in dB that best suits their needs (something the browser could never do for us, because each application has different requirements).\r\n\r\nBut..... Given that GainIndB = 20 * log10(Amplitude) and Amplitude = 10 ^ (GainIndB/20), it should be fairly simple to implement a proper logarithmic control directly in the UI. In fact, [this is exactly what I do in my own web player](https://github.com/carlosrafaelgn/FPlayWeb/blob/main/scripts/player/player.ts#L260). 😊\r\n\r\nI do not have inside information (W3C, WHATWG and so on...). But this is what I believe, considering this issue has been around for over 3 years now. 😅",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
