    "created_at": "2026-08-16T18:06:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-16T18:06:01Z",
    "body": "The impression I'm getting now is the existing field needs to keep its existing vague semantics in case it's being passed opaquely to an OS volume mixer... so instead of adding one new utility getter/setter for logarithmic, perhaps what should be done here is adding _two_ of them, one for guaranteed-linear and one for logarithmic. Maybe they stack instead of all modifying a single value.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
